152 Experiment 1: Small-scale laboratory setting
153 In November 2021, a production crate with ~7.5 kg feed and ~11.200 seed larvae was ran154 domly taken from the production facility at ENORM Biofactory A/S, Denmark, and transpor155 ted for 1 hour to the research facilities of the Department of Biology, Aarhus University, Den156 mark. Upon arrival, feed and larvae were mixed and dosed in 7 round 1 L plastic chambers as 157 part of a small-scale respirometry setup (Figure 2). The 7 replicates contained 408 ± 13 g mix 158 of feed and larvae with similar larval density as in the large-scale experiments (~600 larvae 159 per chamber). The 7 respirometry chambers plus an empty control chamber were placed in a 160 35°C temperature-controlled cabinet and connected to an open-flow respirometry system al161 lowing for hourly measurements of CO2 production rate and O2 consumption rate during the 162 subsequent 7-day growth period (see below for details about small-scale respirometry sys163 tem). The substrate rearing temperature averaged ~35°C with fluctuations confined between 164 33-38°C. At the termination of the experiment larvae from each replicate were weighed and 165 sub-samples of larvae and frass were stored at -20°C for measurements of fractional water, 166 crude lipid, and crude protein content. 167
