386 Discussion 387
388 Comparison of growth and metabolism at large- and small-scale
389 The data from the present study indicated that small-scale laboratory respirometry chambers 390 support gas exchange, growth, and metabolism in BSFL that is comparable, and therefore rep391 resentative of, conditions in large-scale commercial conditions. This finding is based on our 392 efforts to evaluate the utility and relevance of controlled laboratory studies in relation to large393 scale facilities. Specifically, BSFL were reared at similar substrate temperature (~34-35°C) 394 and in similar diets in either small-scale controlled laboratory respiration chambers (~0.4 kg) 395 (Figure 2) or in the larger and more heterogeneous conditions that exist in a rearing unit at 396 ENORM Biofactory A/S (Figure 1) containing >20.000 times more feed and larvae in the sys397 tem. Despite the massive difference in scale, we found remarkable similarities in growth and 398 energy conversion. Thus, survival, individual larval size, % dry mass, % crude lipid, % crude 399 protein, and final larval mass as a proportion of initial mass all differed by less than 10%


